{"kind":"task","id":".verify-flip-implement-snippet-detector","title":"Verify (FLIP 0.03): implement: snippet detector (Caroline + Ingrid)","description":"## FLIP Verification\n\nFLIP score 0.03 is below threshold 0.70 — independently verify this task.\n\n### Original Task\n**ID:** implement-snippet-detector\n**Title:** implement: snippet detector (Caroline + Ingrid)\n**Description:**\n\n```wg-contract\ntouch-set: [src/paia_supernote/snippet_detector.py, tests/test_snippet_detector.py]\nverify: uv run pytest tests/test_snippet_detector.py -v\n```\n\n```specdrift\nspec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-14-paia-supernote-design.md\ncheck: does detector correctly route LFW changes to Caroline, Synth changes to Ingrid? does it only trigger on snippets, not tasks or general notes?\n```\n\nImplement snippet_detector.py — reviews LFW.note and Synth.note for strategy fragments Braydon has written.\n\nTriggered by: watcher fires on LFW.note or Synth.note change → reader transcribes → snippet_detector evaluates.\n\nRouting:\n- LFW.note changes → Caroline\n- Synth.note changes → Ingrid\n\nWhat counts as a snippet (LLM-classified):\n- Incomplete strategic thought\n- Named client/project with an open question\n- Meeting prep that lacks context\n- Something relevant to an active workstream\n\nWhat does NOT trigger:\n- Fully formed notes\n- Task items (□/○ markers — those go to task system)\n- General journaling\n\nBehavior when snippet detected:\n1. Classify text via Claude (claude-sonnet-4-6): snippet / task / general\n2. If snippet: emit supernote.snippet_detected {notebook, page, text, agent}\n3. Agent (Caroline/Ingrid) receives event, initiates browser clarification conversation\n4. After discussion, agent fires supernote.write_requested to write clarified thinking back\n5. Also posts transcription to folio\n\nNote: the browser conversation initiation is the agent's responsibility after receiving snippet_detected. This module only classifies and emits.\n\nTests:\n1. LFW.note change routes to Caroline (agent='caroline')\n2. Synth.note change routes to Ingrid (agent='ingrid')\n3. Task content (□ markers) classified as 'task' not 'snippet'\n4. Strategy fragment classified as 'snippet'\n5. General note classified as 'general' — no event emitted\n\nFile: src/paia_supernote/snippet_detector.py\n\n\n### Verification Instructions\nYou must independently verify whether the work was actually completed.\nDo NOT trust the original agent's claims. Check independently:\n\n1. Check `git log --oneline -10` for recent commits related to this task\n2. Check `git diff` to see if meaningful changes were made\n3. Run `cargo build && cargo test` to verify nothing is broken\n4. Verify any artifacts mentioned in the task description exist\n\n### Verdict\n- If verification **passes**: run `wg log 'implement-snippet-detector' \"FLIP verification passed (score 0.03)\"` and mark this task done.\n- If verification **fails**: run `wg fail 'implement-snippet-detector' --reason \"FLIP verification failed: <reason>\"` then mark this task done.\n","status":"failed","priority":10,"assigned":"agent-897","tags":["verification","agency","eval-scheduled"],"created_at":"2026-04-27T15:17:29.867413+00:00","started_at":"2026-04-27T15:20:40.936621+00:00","log":[{"timestamp":"2026-04-27T15:20:40.936627+00:00","actor":"agent-897","message":"Spawned by wg spawn --executor claude --model opus"},{"timestamp":"2026-04-27T15:21:31.569640+00:00","actor":"agent-897","message":"Task marked as failed: Agent exited with code 1"}],"retry_count":1,"max_retries":1,"failure_reason":"Agent exited with code 1","model":"opus","exec_mode":"light"}
