{"kind":"task","id":".verify-implement-vision-reader","title":"Verify (FLIP 0.45): implement: vision reader (reader.py)","description":"## FLIP Verification & Repair\n\nFLIP score 0.45 is below threshold 0.70 — independently verify and, if needed, **fix** this task's work.\n\n### Your Authority\nYou are a **senior engineer reviewing a junior's PR**. You have full authority to:\n- Edit source files, run builds, run tests, and commit fixes\n- Correct mistakes, resolve test failures, and improve the implementation\n- Only reject (fail) the source task if the approach is fundamentally wrong\n\n**Fix first, fail last.** If the work is close but has issues, repair it yourself.\n\n### Original Task\n**ID:** implement-vision-reader\n**Title:** implement: vision reader (reader.py)\n**Description:**\n\n```wg-contract\ntouch-set: [src/paia_supernote/reader.py, tests/test_reader.py]\nverify: uv run pytest tests/test_reader.py -v\n```\n\n```specdrift\nspec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-14-paia-supernote-design.md\ncheck: does reader extract changed pages only? does checkbox diff detect newly-checked boxes? does classification distinguish task/snippet/general?\n```\n\nImplement reader.py — processes a changed .note file and extracts meaning.\n\nBehavior:\n1. Load .note file via supernotelib.load_notebook()\n2. Extract modified pages as PNG via ImageConverter.convert(page_num)\n3. Transcribe text via Claude vision API (claude-sonnet-4-6, messages with image content block)\n4. Diff checkbox state vs prior snapshot (stored as JSON per notebook per page):\n   - Detect □/○ markers and whether they are checked (■/● or X'd)\n   - newly_checked: list of {task_text, tag (focus/orbit), page_num}\n5. Classify page content:\n   - 'task': contains □/○ markers (handled by task page system)\n   - 'snippet': strategy fragment, client mention, open question (LLM classification)\n   - 'general': everything else\n6. Return: ReadResult(notebook, page_num, text, checkboxes, content_type, timestamp)